{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"- P1 `test/dao/stream/slice_peer.cljc:59` — `stdout.writeln` only queues an asynchronous `IOSink` write, but `:exit` immediately calls `io/exit` at line 155. Dart does not flush pending asynchronous writes before `exit`, so the promised `{:reply :exit}` can be lost under pipe backpressure. Closing stdin can similarly invoke `exit!` while earlier replies remain buffered. Flush/close stdout asynchronously before termination, or set `exitCode` and allow the event loop to drain.\n\n- P2 `test/dao/stream/slice_peer.cljc:180` — The Dart stdin splitter retains every unterminated chunk in `pending` without a maximum frame size. A missing newline or oversized command therefore causes unbounded string growth and repeated whole-buffer copying in `feed!`, potentially exhausting the peer before Transit decoding. Enforce a bounded line size and terminate or report a protocol error when exceeded."}}
